      en: "Windsor Nature Park, opened in 2017, covers 75 hectares in northern Singapore, acting as a buffer zone for the Central Catchment Nature Reserve. The park features 4 km of trails through secondary forest, including the Dillenia Trail and Heritage Boardwalk. It is a birdwatching hotspot, with species such as the Crimson Sunbird and the Red-crowned Barbet. The 2.4 km elevated Windsor Walk provides canopy-level views. The park also has a stream habitat supporting dragonflies and frogs. Facilities include a car park and picnic areas.",
