      en: "The Singapore River is 3.2 km long, flowing from the Central Area to the Marina Bay. It was the heart of Singapore's trading port since Sir Stamford Raffles founded the settlement in 1819. The riverfront features historical quays: Boat Quay, Clarke Quay, and Robertson Quay, now lined with dining and nightlife venues. A massive cleanup in the 1970s transformed the river from a polluted waterway into a clean recreational area. Boat tours operate daily, passing landmarks like the Merlion Park and the Esplanade.",
